name: reference_cdp_tldraw_editor_and_active_leaf
description: "CDP canvas scenarios — scope DOM queries to the active leaf (other sessions leave canvas tabs open), get the tldraw editor via React fiber from .tl-canvas, and DiscourseToolPanel reuses .tlui-style-panel"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: reference
  originSessionId: 1c6f6086-29a4-4359-b62b-67212ac0d346
  modified: 2026-10-01T01:18:23.017Z
---

Obsidian canvas scenarios driven over CDP (`dg-obsidian-cdp-verify`):

- Other sessions leave hidden canvas tabs open. `document.querySelector(".tl-canvas")` and `getLeavesOfType("tldraw-dg-preview")[0]` then hit the wrong canvas. Scope every query to `app.workspace.activeLeaf.view.containerEl`.
- The tldraw editor isn't exposed on the view. To reach it, walk `__reactFiber$*` `.return` up from `.tl-canvas` until `memoizedProps.value.putExternalContent` exists. Starting from `.tl-container` fails because it sits above the EditorContext provider.
- `editor.putExternalContent({ type: "url", url: "obsidian://open?vault=…&file=…" })` drops a node card through the plugin's real drop handler.
- `DiscourseToolPanel` uses the `tlui-style-panel` class. To assert that "no stock style panel" shows, count panels (expect 1); presence alone proves nothing.
- The dev vault's local relations use orphaned relation types, so build a `_verify` fixture (two notes plus one relation of a configured type) and restore `relations.json`.

Related: [[reference_obsidian_cdp_canvas_narrow_breakpoint]], [[reference_cdp_verify_harness_contract]], [[reference_obsidian_orphaned_relation_types]].
